  - spec-bloat
---

## Issues

- [ ] `description` is 171 chars (under cap, fine).

- [ ] `intent` is 86 words (under cap, fine).

- [ ] `outcomes.desired` has 5 items (cap 4). Items 4-5 collapse. Outcome 0
  names the module by name — function/symbol names forbidden in outcomes.
  Traces to: `outcomes.desired` | Brevity Contract caps + Forbidden content (function/symbol names)
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity, Forbidden-content

- [ ] `outcomes.undesired` has 6 paragraph-length items. Cap 3-4, ≤2 sentences.
  Traces to: `outcomes.undesired` | Brevity Contract caps
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity

- [ ] `## Strategy` enumerates module names (`writeMethodology`, `scaffoldCommands`,
  `installMethodologyDocs`) — function names forbidden.
  Traces to: `## Strategy` | Forbidden content
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Forbidden-content

- [ ] `## Good examples` and `## Bad examples` reference exact paths
  (`docs/aide-spec.md`, `docs/commands/aide/`, `docs/progressive-disclosure.md`)
  — file paths forbidden.
  Traces to: examples sections | Forbidden content (file paths)
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Forbidden-content

- [ ] Carry-forward (prior cycle): 3 unchecked items re stale-path drift.
  Re-walk after rewrite.

## Retro

initContent is one of the better-bounded specs structurally but trips the
forbidden-content scan on function names and file paths. The chokepoint
invariant ("install service has exactly one reader of `.aide/docs/`") is
the right level of commitment; the specific function names that participate
live in code with JSDoc references.
